id: pm-v3umtp
title: "GH-1112: Windows Node 24 merge-receipt boundary test relies on POSIX name-length failure"
description: "The scheduled Nightly Validation run 32809906959 failed on windows-latest / Node 24 because merge-receipts.spec.ts expects an overlong receipt filename to reject with ENAMETOOLONG, but the Windows filesystem accepts the constructed path and the promise resolves. The regression test therefore measures a host filesystem limit instead of the merge-receipt contract."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[9]: "area:ci","area:sdk","area:tests",cross-platform,"gh:1112",merge-receipts,nightly,node24,windows
created_at: "2026-08-25T06:08:21.321Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-25T08:01:21.926Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-25T07:06:04.857Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-25T07:06:04.857Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "The damaged-receipt negative control fails deterministically on every supported OS without depending on host filename limits; the production receipt reader still ignores unreadable, invalid, and oversized evidence safely; focused merge-receipt tests pass locally; an exact-head Windows Node 24 workflow proves the regression; GitHub issue #1112 links the canonical PM item"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub issue #1112
severity: high
environment: "windows-latest / Node 24, Nightly Validation run 32809906959, main fb094d038"
repro_steps: "Run tests/unit/sdk/merge-receipts.spec.ts on windows-latest / Node 24; the test is a safe no-op outside Git and ignores damaged receipt files, but its ENAMETOOLONG assertion resolves because Windows accepts the filename."
resolution: Validate the trusted receipt settlement input immediately after Git-directory resolution and before receipt filename construction or file I/O; retain the outside-Git no-op contract and existing settlement/health behavior.
expected_result: "Malformed merge-receipt evidence is rejected with the same schema error on Linux, Windows, and other supported hosts before filesystem access."
actual_result: "markMergeReceiptReconciled constructed and inspected a path from the unvalidated receipt id first, producing ENAMETOOLONG on Linux while the Windows Node 24 nightly resolved the promise."
affected_version: 2026.8.25
component: SDK merge receipt tests
regression: true
customer_impact: The scheduled Windows gate is red and creates a release-trust incident even though the merge-receipt product behavior did not regress.
